  "headline": "Sodium chloride is not on FDA's current shortage list; the earlier shortage was first posted 2018-06-21 and is resolved",
  "headline_cites": ["D35"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's records show sodium chloride is not on the current shortage list as of 2026-10-21; an earlier shortage was first posted on 2018-06-21 and has since been resolved.",
      "cites": ["D35"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspected multiple plants that supply sodium chloride, including Hospira, Inc. (FEI 1021343, 1925262) and Pfizer Healthcare India Private Limited (FEI 3008316085), with inspection outcomes ranging from VAI to OAI and warning letters issued between 2010 and 2025.",
      "cites": ["D11", "D12", "D13", "D14", "D15", "D16", "D17", "D18", "D19", "D20", "D21", "D22", "D23", "D24", "D25", "D26", "D27", "D28", "D29", "D30", "D31", "D32", "D33", "D34"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product used at Corvale Lakeside and Corvale East (NDC 00264180031) is labeled by B. Braun Medical Inc. and manufactured at a B BRAUN plant.",
      "cites": ["E10", "E2", "E18"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 349 units of sodium chloride 9 mg/mL, 50 mL with 9.2 days on hand; Corvale Lakeside holds 117 units with 16.7 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D2", "D4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The top-ranked option is to transfer 18 units of 9 mg/mL, 50 mL from Corvale Lakeside to Corvale East, which would leave Corvale Lakeside with 14 days and bring Corvale East to 10 days.",
      "cites": ["D36"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Alternate manufacturers not on FDA's shortage list today include Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA Inc. (last inspection NAI 2026-05-13) and Medefil, Inc.",
      "cites": ["D37", "D38"]
    }
  ]
}
